## Tool versions and updates

Development tools use `~` ranges in `package.json`: the tested patch is the
minimum, later patches in the same minor are allowed. With coverage enabled,
Vitest and its coverage provider stay at the same exact version because the
provider requires a matching Vitest version. The committed lockfile records
exact resolved versions; frozen CI installs do not pick up newer patches.
Run tools through the project scripts so local and CI checks use the same tools.

`.womm-template.json` records the generator, template version and original
choices. It is provenance, not a list of the tools currently installed.

To update within a range, run `{% if package_manager == 'npm' %}npm update TOOL{% elif package_manager == 'pnpm' %}pnpm update TOOL{% elif package_manager == 'yarn' %}yarn up -R TOOL{% else %}bun update TOOL{% endif %}` and review the lockfile changes.
Before moving to another minor, change the dependency range and review the
release notes for configuration changes. Update Vitest and its coverage
provider together when coverage is enabled.
{% if tooling == "biome" %}{% if package_manager == "yarn" %}Yarn Plug'n'Play has no `node_modules` schema path. This configuration omits
`$schema`; Biome still validates it using the installed tool's own schema.
{% else %}The Biome `$schema` points at the installed package, so it follows patch
updates automatically.
{% endif %}For configuration migrations, run the installed Biome's `migrate` command
to preview changes before applying them with `--write`.
{% endif %}Run all quality, test and build checks before committing the updated
configuration and lockfile. Upgrading WOMM does not update this project's files.

